h2('Fixed Cost Allocation Problem (Case Study - Farm Produce June 2022 P22)')
body('Q: Explain one problem of allocating fixed costs to individual products. [3]')
sp()
body('A:')
bullet('[K] Fixed cost allocation means dividing shared overhead costs among different products or departments.')
bullet('[An] The allocation method chosen is often arbitrary (e.g., based on floor space, labour hours, or sales value), and different methods give different results. [An] This means a product might appear profitable under one allocation method but unprofitable under another. This can lead to incorrect decisions such as dropping a product that actually makes a positive contribution to fixed costs.')
