h2('Trade Union Impact (20-mark set)')
body('Q: Explain two ways a trade union might impact a business. [4]')
sp()
body('A:')
bullet('[K] A trade union is an organisation of workers that collectively bargains with employers over pay, conditions, and workplace issues.')
bullet('[An] Impact 1 - Higher labour costs: Unions negotiate collectively for higher wages and better benefits than individual workers might achieve alone. [An] This increases costs for the business, potentially reducing profit or requiring higher prices that reduce competitiveness.')
bullet('[An] Impact 2 - Improved communication: Unions provide a formal channel for employee concerns to reach management. [An] This can actually benefit the business by identifying problems early, reducing individual grievances, and creating a more stable workforce with lower turnover. However, it also means management must consult and negotiate rather than impose changes unilaterally.')
sp()

h2('Managers\' Contribution in Hospital (Nov 2024 P13 Q6b)')
body('Q: Evaluate how managers contribute to the success of a hospital. [11]')
sp()
body('A:')
bullet('[K] Managers plan, organise, direct, and control the activities of the hospital to achieve its objectives (patient care, efficiency, financial viability).')
bullet('[An] FOR: Effective resource allocation: Hospital managers ensure limited resources (beds, staff, equipment, budgets) are allocated where most needed. [An] Good management means shorter waiting times, appropriate staffing levels, and efficient use of expensive medical equipment, directly improving patient outcomes.')
bullet('[An] FOR: Staff coordination and motivation: Managers coordinate large, diverse teams (doctors, nurses, administrators, cleaners). [An] Good management creates clear communication, resolves conflicts, ensures training, and motivates staff, leading to better teamwork and patient care.')
bullet('[An] FOR: Strategic planning: Managers plan for future needs (ageing population, new treatments, facility upgrades). [An] Without forward planning, the hospital would be unable to adapt to changing healthcare demands and government requirements.')
bullet('[An] AGAINST: However, excessive management layers can create bureaucracy that slows clinical decisions. [An] Doctors and nurses may feel constrained by management targets that focus on cost reduction rather than patient care. Over-management can demotivate clinical professionals.')
bullet('[An] AGAINST: Management costs consume resources that could fund frontline patient care. [An] Every dollar spent on management salaries is a dollar not spent on nurses, equipment, or treatments.')
bullet('[Ev] JUDGEMENT: Good management is essential for hospital success - healthcare is too complex and resource-constrained to operate without coordination and planning. However, the management approach must be appropriate: clinical professionals need autonomy within a managed framework, and management should support rather than obstruct patient care. The best hospital managers combine business skills with understanding of healthcare priorities.')
sp()

h2('Recruitment Recommendation (Case Study - Cartoon Costumes Nov 2022 P22)')
