body('A:')
bullet('[App/An] Social media marketing: CP can use platforms like Instagram and TikTok to showcase children playing with products, reaching parents where they spend time online. [An] This is relatively low cost, highly targeted (can target parents of specific age children), and allows sharing/viral spread. User-generated content of happy children is powerful social proof.')
bullet('[App/An] Point-of-sale displays in retail stores: Colourful, attractive displays near checkouts or in toy aisles catch the attention of both children and parents. [An] This influences impulse purchases at the moment of decision, when the customer is already in a buying mindset. Demonstration units allow children to try products, increasing desire.')
sp()

h2('Promotion Methods (Case Study - Priya\'s Bookshop June 2022 P21)')
body('Q: Explain two methods of promotion suitable for PB. [4]')
sp()
body('A:')
bullet('[App/An] Social media presence: Creating engaging content about books, reading recommendations, author events, and shop atmosphere. [An] This builds a community of book lovers, is low cost, and reaches local customers effectively. Regular posts keep PB visible and encourage visits.')
bullet('[App/An] Author events and book signings: Hosting local authors creates unique experiences that online retailers cannot match. [An] Events attract new customers, generate local press coverage, and create social media content. They position PB as a community hub rather than just a shop, building loyalty.')
