h1('16. MARKETING MIX - PLACE')
body('Supply chain management, distribution channels.')
sp()

h2('Supply Chain Management (Case Study - Fruit Farm March 2023 P22)')
body('Q: Explain the importance of supply chain management for FF. [4]')
sp()
body('A:')
bullet('[K] Supply chain management (SCM) involves coordinating and managing all activities involved in sourcing, procurement, production, and delivery of products to customers.')
bullet('[App/An] Fresh produce is perishable: FF must manage the time from harvest to customer very carefully. [An] Poor SCM means fruit spoils in transit, leading to waste, customer complaints, and lost revenue. Effective SCM ensures cold chain integrity and rapid delivery, maintaining freshness and quality.')
bullet('[App/An] Coordinating multiple distribution channels: FF may sell to supermarkets, local markets, and direct to consumers. [An] SCM ensures the right quantities are delivered to the right places at the right times, preventing oversupply (waste) to some channels and undersupply (lost sales) to others.')
sp()

h2('Marketing Mix for New Product (Case Study - Plasshape Nov 2023 P21)')
body('Q: Recommend an appropriate marketing mix for PS launching a new plastic product. [6]')
sp()
body('A:')
bullet('[App] Product: Must be functional, durable, and meet customer specifications. If selling to other businesses (B2B), technical quality and reliability are paramount. If consumer-facing, design and aesthetics matter more.')
bullet('[App] Price: For a new product from an established manufacturer, competitive pricing signals value while not undermining quality perception. If the product has unique features, moderate price skimming may be possible.')
bullet('[App] Promotion: B2B approach likely most effective - trade exhibitions, direct sales teams visiting potential customers, technical specifications shared with procurement departments. Trade journal advertising. Digital presence with detailed product information.')
bullet('[App] Place: Direct sales for large orders (relationship-based), distributors for wider market access. Online ordering system for repeat purchases.')
bullet('[Ev] The specific mix depends on whether PS is targeting business or consumer markets. B2B requires emphasis on product quality, direct relationships, and competitive pricing. Consumer markets require greater promotional investment and retail distribution.')
sp()

h2('SCM for Internet Retailer (June 2024 P13 Q6b)')
body('Q: Evaluate the importance of supply chain management for an internet retailer. [11]')
sp()
body('A:')
bullet('[K] SCM coordinates the flow of goods from suppliers through to customers.')
bullet('[An] FOR: Customer expectations of speed. [An] Online shoppers expect fast delivery (often next-day or same-day). Effective SCM ensures inventory is available in distribution centres near customers, carriers are reliable, and systems track deliveries accurately. Poor SCM means late deliveries, wrong items, and customer loss to Amazon and similar competitors with excellent logistics.')
bullet('[An] FOR: Cost management. [An] Delivery is a major cost for internet retailers. Efficient SCM optimises routes, consolidates shipments, negotiates carrier rates, and minimises returns costs. Poor SCM with inefficient logistics erodes already thin online retail margins.')
bullet('[An] FOR: Inventory management. [An] Holding too much stock ties up cash; too little means stockouts and lost sales. SCM systems using demand data optimise inventory levels, reducing waste while maintaining availability.')
bullet('[An] AGAINST: However, SCM is largely about execution rather than competitive advantage. [An] If all internet retailers have good SCM (which market leaders do), it becomes a necessity rather than a differentiator. The retailer still needs strong product range, pricing, and marketing to attract customers in the first place.')
bullet('[An] AGAINST: Heavy investment in SCM infrastructure (warehouses, technology, vehicles) requires significant capital. [An] Small internet retailers may be unable to invest in own logistics, relying on third-party carriers over whom they have limited control.')
bullet('[Ev] JUDGEMENT: SCM is critically important for an internet retailer because delivery IS the customer experience (unlike physical retail where the shop visit is the experience). Poor logistics directly cause customer loss. However, SCM alone does not create success - it must be combined with strong product proposition, competitive pricing, and effective digital marketing. For large retailers, investing in own SCM is competitive advantage; for smaller ones, partnering with reliable third-party logistics providers is essential.')
sp()

h2('SCM for Electric Car Manufacturer (June 2023 P11 Q5b)')
body('Q: Evaluate the importance of SCM for an electric car manufacturer. [11]')
sp()
body('A:')
bullet('[K] SCM manages the entire supply chain from raw materials to finished vehicle delivery to customers.')
bullet('[An] FOR: Electric vehicles require specialist components (batteries, electric motors, charging systems) from limited global suppliers. [An] Effective SCM ensures reliable supply of these critical, expensive components. Supply disruption (e.g., lithium shortage for batteries) halts entire production lines, causing massive revenue loss and customer order cancellations.')
bullet('[An] FOR: Quality control across the supply chain is safety-critical. [An] Defective battery components can cause fires or failures. SCM must ensure all suppliers meet strict quality standards through audits, testing, and certification. A single supplier quality failure could trigger expensive recalls and reputational damage.')
bullet('[An] FOR: Cost management in a competitive market. [An] Batteries represent 30-40% of electric vehicle cost. Effective SCM that negotiates good supply contracts, reduces waste, and optimises logistics directly impacts the final vehicle price and competitiveness against rivals.')
bullet('[An] AGAINST: However, other factors also determine success. [An] Vehicle design, technology innovation, brand image, dealer network, and marketing are equally important. The best supply chain cannot sell a poorly designed or overpriced vehicle.')
bullet('[Ev] JUDGEMENT: SCM is exceptionally important for an electric car manufacturer due to the specialist nature of components, limited supplier base, safety requirements, and cost pressures. It is arguably more important than for traditional car manufacturers because the supply chain for EV components is less mature and more vulnerable to disruption. However, it must work alongside strong R&D, marketing, and sales to create a successful business.')
sp()

h2('SCM in Hospital (Nov 2023 P13 Q6b)')
body('Q: Evaluate the importance of supply chain management in a hospital. [11]')
sp()
body('A:')
bullet('[K] Hospital SCM manages the procurement and delivery of medical supplies, pharmaceuticals, equipment, and consumables needed for patient care.')
bullet('[An] FOR: Patient safety depends on supply reliability. [An] If medicines, surgical supplies, or blood products are unavailable when needed, patient health is directly threatened. SCM must ensure critical items are always in stock, with contingency plans for supply disruption.')
bullet('[An] FOR: Cost control in budget-constrained healthcare. [An] Hospitals spend enormous amounts on supplies. Effective SCM negotiates better prices, reduces waste (expired medicines, unused supplies), and consolidates purchasing across departments, freeing budget for frontline patient care.')
bullet('[An] FOR: Managing complexity. [An] Hospitals use thousands of different products from hundreds of suppliers. Without systematic SCM, ordering is chaotic, duplicated, and expensive. Automated systems ensure efficient ordering, storage, and distribution across wards and departments.')
bullet('[An] AGAINST: Clinical priorities must override pure supply chain efficiency. [An] A hospital cannot operate JIT for life-saving medicines - safety stock must be held even if it represents inefficient use of capital. Patient safety always takes priority over cost minimisation.')
bullet('[Ev] JUDGEMENT: SCM is extremely important in hospitals because supply failures have life-or-death consequences and budgets are limited. However, it must be adapted to healthcare priorities - patient safety and clinical needs override pure efficiency. The best hospital SCM balances cost control with reliability, ensuring essential supplies are always available while minimising waste and cost. Technology (automated ordering, barcode tracking, AI demand prediction) is transforming hospital SCM effectiveness.')
sp()

